{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at buried interfaces in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, it reveals simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during processing. The research identifies outward solvent evaporation delaying α-phase conversion at the buried interface, causing kinetic mismatch that worsens moisture damage. A self-segregating molecule (NFA) was designed to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier, achieving 24.84% power conversion efficiency with stable performance after 1000h damp aging.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture damage",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier for moisture resistance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a general strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental trade-offs in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates why early humans settled only briefly in specific desert regions despite abundant water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across Arabia's Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found that the availability of stone for tool production was a critical factor alongside water. Palaeolake deposits existed at 55 of 125 sites, but no lithic artefacts or knappable materials were present where water was accessible. The analysis indicates that early human settlement required both water and lithic resources, not water alone, suggesting that raw-material geology significantly constrains dispersal patterns in arid regions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Palaeolake deposits were present at 55 of 125 surveyed sites in Arabia's Rub' al Khali desert",
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable stone materials were found in areas with abundant water",
    "Spatial modeling shows 57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, improving site discrimination accuracy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings demonstrate that lithic resource availability, not water alone, critically constrained early human dispersal in arid regions, challenging existing models that overestimate habitable ranges for stone-tool-dependent populations."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors like PRKAR1A. Deletion of Prkar1a reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, enhancing PKA signaling and causing gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Prostaglandin activates PKA to upregulate tissue-protective factors in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors (e.g., PRKAR1A) in ILC3s",
    "IL-23 overproduction reduces PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to intestinal inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used quantum gas microscopy to investigate three-flavor Hubbard systems, examining their phase diagram via site- and flavor-resolved detection. It identified flavor-selective localization and selective pairing at low temperatures, with results validated by linked-cluster expansion calculations. The findings suggest potential for observing a pair Mott phase and advancing quantum chromodynamics research.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Flavor-selective localization observed in three-fl. Hubbard systems",
    "Selective pairing mechanisms identified at low temperatures",
    "Validation of results through linked-cluster expansion calculations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The work demonstrates a pathway to observe pair Mott phases and explore quantum chromodynamics phenomena in multi-flavor strongly correlated systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling scalable production of complex 3D architectures. Results show 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid filaments achieve zero volume shrinkage post-sintering, with tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) and mechanical properties.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing enables high-loading nanocomposites (55 wt% boron nitride) with long-range ordered nanostructures",
    "Post-sintering materials exhibit zero volume shrinkage and exceptional thermomechanical stability",
    "Vertically aligned composites show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable method for cross-scale design of nanocomposites with tailored functionalities, advancing thermal management and structural materials applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study used computational simulations of the Drosophila ventral nerve cord connectomes to identify a central pattern generator (CPG) for fly walking. It discovered a minimal three-neuron circuit comprising one inhibitory and two excitatory interneurons that generates rhythmic leg movements across all six legs. The circuit was necessary and sufficient for motor rhythms and was validated through optogenetic experiments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A minimal three-neuron circuit (one inhibitory, two excitatory interneurons) generates rhythmic leg motor activity in flies",
    "This circuit is necessary and sufficient for coordinated rhythmic movement across all six legs",
    "Optogenetic validation confirmed a separate descending pathway (DNb08) drives rhythmic leg movements"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides the first identified cellular and synaptic structure of a central pattern generator for walking in any animal, advancing understanding of rhythmic motor control mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study examines the current landscape of obesity management medications (OMMs), emphasizing the need for rationally developed therapies based on understanding food intake and energy expenditure regulation. It highlights how advances in molecular communication pathways from peripheral organs to the brain have enabled OMMs to achieve sustainable weight loss. However, challenges like side effects, variable treatment responses, and long-term metabolic adaptations may limit existing OMMs, necessitating further medication development for improved obesity outcomes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Advances in molecular communication pathways from peripheral organs to the brain enable rationally designed obesity management medications (OMMs) to achieve sustainable weight loss",
    "Existing OMMs face limitations including side effects, heterogeneous treatment responses, and long-term metabolic adaptations",
    "Further development of OMMs is justified to address these challenges and improve obesity health outcomes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research underscores the importance of targeted molecular mechanisms in obesity management, providing a foundation for developing safer, more effective medications that address the chronic nature of obesity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility in cocatalysts between alkaline water oxidation systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. The researchers developed a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx photocatalyst achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest reported for Ta-based nitrides. Mechanistic insights indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and surface kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of cocatalyst incompatibility between alkaline water oxidation and pure water splitting as a bottleneck for Ta3N5 photocatalysis",
    "Development of a highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst via multi-step incipient wetness impregnation",
    "Optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx achieved 0.72% apparent quantum yield for stoichiometric water splitting at 420 nm"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting over nitride materials, providing mechanistic insights for advancing efficient solar-driven water splitting systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether brief dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term tissue immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a transient high-fat diet (HFD) exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates inflammation comparably to chronic obesity. HFD outside this window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during the window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD recruits neutrophils that express Nlrp3 and Il1b, activating a neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β axis that licenses pathogenic TH17 cells. Post-recovery, chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cells persist, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent low-fat diet. The findings demonstrate that short-term dietary states during specific temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure within a 4-day window at disease onset exacerbates skin inflammation comparably to chronic obesity",
    "HFD outside the 4-day window or switching obese mice to low-fat diet during this window blunts disease amplification",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and NLRP3-IL-1β signaling license pathogenic TH17 cells, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes that transient dietary states during narrow temporal windows can durably reprogram immune responses, revealing a mechanism by which short-lived physiological changes embed into tissue immune memory."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether GLP-1 receptor agonists can be leveraged for addiction treatment, focusing on their potential to improve overall health outcomes. The research explores their mechanism of action in modulating neural pathways associated with substance use. Results indicate these therapies may reduce addiction-related behaviors and enhance metabolic health, suggesting a dual benefit for addiction management and metabolic disorders.",
  "key_findings": [
    "GLP- 1 receptor agonists show promise in reducing addiction-related behaviors",
    "These therapies may improve metabolic health alongside addiction treatment",
    "The approach offers a potential bridge to integrated whole-person health care"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The findings suggest GLP-1 receptor agonists could provide a novel therapeutic strategy for dual management of addiction and metabolic health, advancing integrated care approaches."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a precursor-level design principle for hard-carbon anodes in sodium-ion batteries by regulating asphaltene molecular heterogeneity through cohesion-solvation mechanisms. Toluene-fractionated precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores, yielding high-performance hard carbon with 400.1 mAh g-1 capacity and exceptional cycling stability. The findings demonstrate how molecular selection in heterogeneous feedstocks directly influences structural evolution and electrochemical performance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Toluene-fractionated asphaltene precursors undergo oxidative crosslinking to form turbostratic domains and closed pores",
    "AHC-80-1400 achieves 400.1 mAh g-1 capacity at 0.05 A g-1 with 87.7% initial capacity retention",
    "The hard-carbon exhibits 92.3% capacity retention after 10,000 cycles and wide-temperature stability"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a precursor-stage molecular design principle that enables precise control over hard-carbon structural evolution from heterogeneous feedstocks, advancing sodium-ion battery anode engineering through molecular-level regulation of carbonization pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines bottleneuses in scaling indoor photovoltaic technologies for real-world deployment. It analyzes how low-light conditions favor wide-bandgap absorbers and reduced voltage losses while reshaping module design to minimize series resistance and shunt pathways. The study identifies critical measurement practices and regulatory constraints for transitioning lab-scale devices to practical applications in built environments.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Low-light operation favors wide-bandgap absorbers and reduced non-radiative voltage losses",
    "Lower series resistance permits wider subcells and fewer interconnections, increasing geometric fill factor",
    "Shunt and leakage pathways consume significant photocurrent under low-light conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes critical design principles and measurement standards for scaling indoor photovoltaics from laboratory demonstrations to practical, deployable products in real-world environments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study quantifies anthropogenic noise's global biological impacts through phylogenetic meta-analyses of 214 experiments across 177 species. Noise altered physiological, developmental, or behavioral traits in 80% of species, reducing fitness, abundance, and disrupting predator-prey interactions. Effects were universal across habitats but varied by species and traits, indicating noise as a pervasive selection pressure reshaping ecosystems.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Noise altered physiological, developmental, or behavioral traits in  80% of 177 species studied",
    "Noise reduced fitness and abundance while disrupting predator-prey interactions",
    "Effects occurred universally across habitats but varied by species and traits, creating winners and losers"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This research establishes anthropogenic noise as a novel selection pressure reshaping ecosystem dynamics, necessitating integrated soundscape conservation strategies alongside traditional habitat protection."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the limitations of conventional biomaterials in treating deep-seated osteomyelitis by developing programmable engineered living vehicles (ELVs) that autonomously navigate to infection sites. These ELVs, based on self-propelled E. coli Nissle 1917, deploy temperature-responsive genetic circuits to produce bacteriolytic lysostaphin and vasoactive intestinal peptide. The ELVs penetrate biofilms, clear MRSA infections more effectively than vancomycin, and accelerate bone regeneration through localized immune modulation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ELVs autonomously navigate to infected niches in rat osteomyelitis models",
    "Temperature-responsive genetic circuits produce lysostaphin and VIP ≥37°C",
    "ELVs outperform vancomycin in MRSA clearance and accelerate bone repair"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a programmable living vehicle platform that integrates synthetic biology with micro-engineering to enable autonomous biofactory functions for complex infections and tissue regeneration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study establishes precise metrology for attosecond hard X-ray pulses using a broadband X-ray split-delay line. Field-correlation measurements characterized pulse coherence time, while non-sequential two-photon absorption quantified average pulse duration at 170 as. The approach enables time-resolved experiments like X-ray pump-probe spectroscopy and diffraction, advancing sub-ångström spatial and attosecond temporal resolution for observing electron dynamics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Field-correlation measurements provided first time-domain characterization of pulse coherence time",
    "Non-sequential two-photon absorption quantified average pulse duration as 170 as",
    "The technique enables systematic attosecond time-resolved experiments including X-ray pump-probe spectroscopy"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes attosecond hard X-ray pulse metrology, enabling direct observation of electron motion with sub-ångström spatial and attosecond temporal resolution."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how tumor metastasis induces immunosuppression by co-opting liver hematopoiesis. Using mouse models, researchers identified metastasis-associated hematopoietic stem cells (LM-HSCs) that establish ectopic hematopoietic niches in the liver. These LM-HSCs differentiate into glucocorticoid-producing neutrophils, which suppress CD8+ T and NK cell activity via paracrine glucocorticoid signaling. The findings reveal a mechanism by which metastases promote immunosuppression through hepatic hematopoiet. (58 words)",
  "key_findings": [
    "Liver metastases establish ectopic hematopoietic niches via LM-HSCs",
    "LM-HSCs differentiate into glucocorticoid-producing ANXA1+ neutrophils",
    "These neutrophils induce immune checkpoint expression and T/NK cell anergy through glucocorticoid signaling"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a novel mechanism by which tumor metastases reprogram hepatic hematopoiesis to suppress antitumor immunity, providing insights into immunosuppressive tumor microenvironments."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates liquid metal inks for stretchable electronics, addressing activation-dependent conductivity and electrical instability under strain. The researchers engineered an island-bridge microstructure using Cu-decorated carbon nanotubes bridging liquid metal particles via hydrogen bonding and coordination. The ink maintains high conductivity (1.3 × 10^-1 Ω sq^-1) at 300% strain and enables high-resolution electromyography with machine learning for real-time exercise state monitoring.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Intrinsically conductive liquid metal ink with island-bridge microstructure",
    "Retains 1.3 × 10^-1 Ω sq^-1 sheet resistance at 300% strain",
    "Machine learning-enhanced electromyography for exercise state monitoring"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work advances scalable liquid metal electronics with strain-resilient conductive networks for intelligent wearable biointerfaces."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the molecular basis of the female protective effect (FPE) in autism spectrum disorder (ASD). Using human neural progenitor cells, researchers identified transcriptomic convergence among 18 ASD genes, revealing shared downregulation of ASD genes. De novo reconstruction of a gene regulatory network highlighted CHD8 and REST as key transcriptional regulators, while X-linked ZFX emerged as a critical factor that may buffer ASD gene mutations in females, explaining the FPE.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transcriptomic convergence of 18 ASD genes in human neural progenitor cells",
    "CHD8 and REST identified as central transcriptional regulators driving gene expression changes",
    "X-linked ZFX expression buffers ASD gene mutations in females, contributing to the female protective effect"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides molecular mechanisms underlying the female protective effect in ASD by demonstrating how gene regulatory networks converge upon ASD gene disruption and how X-linked ZFX expression may mitigate genetic risk."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates adipose tissue plasticity in response to physiological demands, examining how remodeling processes coordinate metabolic, structural, and functional adaptations. The research identifies that coordinated changes in adipocyte metabolism, extracellular matrix, vascularization, immune composition, and innervation maintain tissue homeostasis. Pathological remodeling in obesity and cancer promotes disease progression through fibroinflammatory niches and tissue disruption, highlighting the need for targeted interventions beyond fat reduction.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Coordinated adipose remodeling preserves energy buffering, thermogenesis, and endocrine function under physiological stress",
    "Pathological remodeling in obesity drives disease complications via fibroinflammatory niches",
    "Tumor-associated adipose tissue promotes cancer growth through metabolic reprogramming and tissue invasion"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes adipose tissue plasticity as a central mechanism in both physiological adaptation and disease pathogenesis, emphasizing the necessity of targeting tissue-specific remodeling processes for therapeutic interventions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates polarization-insensitive, broadband metasurface holograph. It employs monolithic 3D printing with height-coded resin pillars to create a low-index metasurface that operates across visible wavelengths and spatial channels. The device generates dual-credential authentication via far-field public keys and wavelength/distance-selective near-field passwords without polarization optics, demonstrating compact spectral-spatial meta-authentication.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Monolithically 3D-printed metasurface achieves polarization-insensitive broadband holography across visible wavelengths",
    "Height-coded resin pillars enable a single phase map for multi-wavelength operation without polarization dependence",
    "Device provides dual-credential optical authentication using far-field public keys and near-field passwords under unpolarized light"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a compact, polarization-insensitive metasurface platform for simultaneous spectral and spatial authentication, advancing optical security through integrated wavelength and spatial channel management without external polarization optics."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the demographic origins of Celtic languages using ancient genomic data from 4,587 Bronze and Iron Age European individuals. By analyzing genome-wide data, the researchers identified three key population movements: Steppe-related ancestry arriving via Bell Beaker groups around 4400 BP, a Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain, and a westward expansion of eastern central European ancestry (3200-2800 BP) affecting France, the British Isles, Iberia, and Italy. The findings suggest that the eastern central European migration is the most parsimonious explanation for Celtic language spread, despite language shifts not always aligning with genetic changes.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Steppe-related ancestry entered Europe via Bell Beaker-associated groups approximately 4400 years ago",
    "Bronze Age migration from southwestern Europe to Britain occurred between 3800-3200 BP",
    "Eastern central European ancestry expanded westward from 3200-2800 BP, influencing regions where Celtic languages later developed"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides genomic evidence supporting a specific demographic pathway for Celtic language dispersal, clarifying the demographic processes that may have facilitated the spread of Celtic languages across prehistoric Europe."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how noise measurements resolve a long-standing puzzle in high-temperature superconductivity. By analyzing noise characteristics in superconducting systems, researchers identified critical relationships between noise and superconducting properties. The findings suggest that noise can provide insights into the underlying mechanisms of high-temperature superconductivity, potentially clarifying its complex behavior.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Noise measurements reveal critical relationships between noise and superconducting properties",
    "The approach identifies noise as a key factor in understanding high-temperature super:superconductivity",
    "The results indicate noise provides insights into the underlying mechanisms of high-temperature superconductivity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that noise analysis can elucidate fundamental aspects of high-temperature superconductivity, advancing understanding of its complex physical mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing ammonia synthesis from nitrate using electrocatalysis. Researchers developed a MOF-derived Co3O4 catalyst via controlled pyrolysis of Co-MOF- 74, achieving 96.7% Faradaic efficiency and stability across varying pH and nitrate concentrations. Spectroscopic analysis and DFT calculations showed oxygen vacancies induce octahedral Co site distortion, promoting high-spin states that improve nitrate adsorption and electron transfer kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "MOF-derived Co3O4 catalyst achieved 96.7% Faradaic efficiency for nitrate-to-ammonia conversion",
    "Oxygen vacancies in the catalyst caused octahedral Co site distortion, enabling high-spin state transitions",
    "The catalyst maintained stability and activity across a wide pH and nitrate concentration range"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates atomic-scale spin engineering of cobalt sites in MOF-derived catalysts to enhance electrocatalytic nitrate reduction, providing a pathway for energy-efficient ammonia production without CO2 emissions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study develops structRFM, an RNA foundation model trained on 21 million sequence-structure pairs using structure-guided masked language modeling. It integrates base-pairing interactions via pair-matching and employs multi-source ensembles to reduce bias. The model excels in zero-shot homology classification, secondary-using prediction, and tertiary structure modeling, matching AlphaFold3 performance on key benchmarks while generalizing to novel RNA families and long non-coding RNAs.",
  "key_findings": [
    "structRFM achieves high performance in zero-shot homology classification without task-specific training",
    "The model improves tertiary structure prediction with Zfold, matching AlphaFold3 across multiple benchmark datasets",
    "structRFM generalizes effectively to newly released RNA families and long non-coding RNAs"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes structure-guided pre-training as a robust strategy for RNA foundation models, advancing capabilities for accurate structural and functional inference across diverse RNA types."
}
